# Archiving a plan

A built plan moves to `{{ARCHIVE_DIR}}` under the same file name. Every path that names it moves with
it, or the next reader follows a dead link.

## When

| The plan | Do |
|---|---|
| Built, and its header or the pull request says so | archive it |
| A dated investigation whose live list is elsewhere ({{OPEN_LIST}}) | archive it, and name the live list in the status line |
| Not built, not scheduled | leave it with a "Parked" line |
| Steps for one past operation (a merge, a migration) | remove it only when {{PEOPLE}} says so; git keeps it |
| Partly built, with decisions still open | check each against the code; put what is still open in {{OPEN_LIST}}, then archive |

Deletes happen only on the word of {{PEOPLE}}.

## Steps

1. Check the plan against the code. What it says was built, is it there? Name what is still open.
2. Move it: `git mv {{PLANS_DIR}}/<f>.md {{ARCHIVE_DIR}}/<f>.md`. A dated doc from elsewhere gets a dated
   name: `{{ARCHIVE_DIR}}/YYYY-MM-DD-<topic>.md`.
3. Add a status line under its title:
   `> **Archived YYYY-MM-DD.** Built … (where). Still open: … (in {{OPEN_LIST}}).`
   A parked plan gets `> **Parked, YYYY-MM-DD.** Not built and not scheduled.`
4. Fix every path that names it: `git grep -n '<f>.md'`.
   - Paths in backticks are written from the repo root: change the folder.
   - Markdown links are relative to the file that holds them; a link inside the moved file may need `../`.
   - Comments in code: fix them in the same commit.{{SKIP_NOTE}}
5. A memory that names the old path is updated in the same turn: change only the path.
6. Lint. Every link must resolve:
   ```sh
   {{AUDIT}}
   ```
   Its "Paths to moved files" lists what still points at the old path. At least
   `git grep -n '{{PLANS_DIR}}/<f>'` must return nothing.
7. One commit per batch: "Docs: archive <n> built records".
